[{:db/id "q-251069/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer/id #uuid "ec7c2c13-0647-5bdf-9602-8d0941c1ae83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251069/field-1/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab" :answer/id #uuid "522ef804-a625-59cc-b29a-59baf4ed2e78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251069/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "61e9bf01-0d9f-50b1-a4c2-8d1af4dc9f92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251069/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer-field/choices ["q-251069/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" "q-251069/field-1/c9ec5d6cdf4e67c7f8bce68475bed400e56bf403f3d09b5928f78b6baa512eab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251069" :question/id #uuid "aadee610-8257-53c0-bdd3-cdaae7e5f633" :question/math-academy-id "q-251069" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/85344df61b503271cd23cb3c741cd659b1417cb34b9031f0283dcf9c8fae6794.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and need to determine the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({20}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AC}{12} \\\\ AC & =12\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({20}^{∘}) \\\\ AC & =4.367…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (4.367…)\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =26.205… \\\\  & ≈26,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251069/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4312362-9961-5bf7-9423-42f4c2f7a13c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251069"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251070/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "7c85af72-d294-53bf-ad87-6c3f84ddb768" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251070/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "db52aa00-509b-5012-a2fb-50707ea4aa2d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251070/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-251070/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251070" :question/id #uuid "2a687ddb-5483-5cff-9ddf-a1874dbba356" :question/math-academy-id "q-251070" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/ed3de6f6fe96fab30d6f3927582a00ee9d0edc1f2514fec17507e2398009217f.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and need to determine the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AC}{5} \\\\ AC & =5\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ AC & =2.886…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2.886…)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =7.216… \\\\  & ≈7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251070/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4312362-9961-5bf7-9423-42f4c2f7a13c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251070"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251064/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "8ef00204-96ac-50b7-860a-ee6c79b1e81c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251064/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af" :answer/id #uuid "18617fe8-c9c0-5389-9dc8-ba1d26fe3faf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251064/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "829ca167-5326-547a-b735-659495b6b1de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251064/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-251064/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-251064/field-1/7845f5bf94d2cfe99f73682a34529955af46f8f5d6f59bb198a07cbc245060af"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251064" :question/id #uuid "3d2f81dd-67ab-5130-8a01-588c2d7dd1e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-251064" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/fbccea4652fde939777bd69f621497f9e63ee79c7d4e4f0a5327bb141ce021ca.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of a right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and need to determine the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =\\frac{6}{BC} \\\\ BC\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =6 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({70}^{∘})} \\\\ BC & =2.183…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot (2.183…) \\\\  & =6.551… \\\\  & ≈7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251064/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4312362-9961-5bf7-9423-42f4c2f7a13c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251064"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251074/field-1/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" :answer/id #uuid "a71591b4-86fd-5e2f-9882-8d1a20f2c845" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "52" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251074/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1ded80de-2cbd-5d3c-a8a1-0bcda5e04703" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251074/field-1/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997" :answer-field/choices ["q-251074/field-1/85f23a53be0e95a7e191561cc5a77501369717526aae5254cc8d13ed8080d997"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251074" :question/id #uuid "117cc85c-6094-519a-9785-f355ef4c8616" :question/math-academy-id "q-251074" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/e72091463bf8f973629ff1467ae8ca184689b4745c387acac618b8a81876c52f.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and need to determine the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AC}{14} \\\\ AC & =14\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) \\\\ AC & =7.443…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (7.443…)\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =52.107… \\\\  & ≈52,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251074/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4312362-9961-5bf7-9423-42f4c2f7a13c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251074"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-28308/selection/0779f4495b7cc2ab405379f3fac874eda363d9d1e4a672e76e3fcbd03d50f77b" :answer/id #uuid "22b1cb37-20ee-52fb-8882-b8b4c2f5c200" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "241" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28308/selection/c8f1fc5bf46fd6d693db422117daa31dc63eabab1ea9a762487c2f7b2d213f1d" :answer/id #uuid "9a9cf4f4-033d-5e68-ae76-6a09fdcadad0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "236" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28308/selection/e8b7e47cca1ef3eb964f0ed7f42d96fd7bfece9e27c46142bc4e5ae957bf6ebd" :answer/id #uuid "dc189ced-daed-5439-a00d-0cfca665c5bc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "245" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28308/selection/f46e55cb5f98696a52a1bd1b9766cfac6721556aa84b78d36870dfcbc2b6d07c" :answer/id #uuid "8d9f080a-f9d3-56ac-a070-100df577f177" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "233" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28308/selection/8747f67f954041f89c5523cf65d5c9b793558dc62b419a5e3cc329c864c091bc" :answer/id #uuid "17984ca8-7d3a-5510-8343-726a4e82c6c5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "238" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28308/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "46230c9e-658d-5100-bb7f-79917ee1b44e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-28308/selection/8747f67f954041f89c5523cf65d5c9b793558dc62b419a5e3cc329c864c091bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-28308/selection/0779f4495b7cc2ab405379f3fac874eda363d9d1e4a672e76e3fcbd03d50f77b" "q-28308/selection/c8f1fc5bf46fd6d693db422117daa31dc63eabab1ea9a762487c2f7b2d213f1d" "q-28308/selection/e8b7e47cca1ef3eb964f0ed7f42d96fd7bfece9e27c46142bc4e5ae957bf6ebd" "q-28308/selection/f46e55cb5f98696a52a1bd1b9766cfac6721556aa84b78d36870dfcbc2b6d07c" "q-28308/selection/8747f67f954041f89c5523cf65d5c9b793558dc62b419a5e3cc329c864c091bc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-28308" :question/id #uuid "f806f6d9-b146-5a87-9874-1eb64a7a1553" :question/math-academy-id "q-28308" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/43e5ba6bff8a20c20f8be2b18d57ad07fc030477d589a2ba43da0f2cb3816587.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of $△ABC$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and need to determine the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({40}^{∘}) & =\\frac{20}{BC} \\\\ BC\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({40}^{∘}) & =20 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{20}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({40}^{∘})} \\\\ BC & =23.835…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 20\\cdot (23.835…) \\\\  & =238.350… \\\\  & ≈238,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-28308/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4312362-9961-5bf7-9423-42f4c2f7a13c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-28308"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251078/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "1c4f597d-80b6-54bb-b310-968ef151ea20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251078/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5002344a-229b-5afb-8703-6daff5817d3a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251078/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer-field/choices ["q-251078/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251078" :question/id #uuid "f18363ef-03d9-5502-922b-35e61fbd60b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-251078" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/7acf00fc8ac1ac67612b740450fe62f7cddee2a9fc7a9c28fe54fafb2c1ee57c.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{5}{2},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{5}{2}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & =\\frac{3x-1}{12-5x} \\\\ 5(12-5x) & =2(3x-1) \\\\ 60-25x & =6x-2 \\\\ 31x & =62 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =12-5x=12-5(2)=2, \\\\ AC & =3x-1=3(2)-1=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251078/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251078"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251089/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "600b45b3-9266-5373-85b7-d2067f0f81ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251089/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "4e44e423-5df9-50ca-b8ea-ec0d624532cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251089/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed72c7f2-e36a-56d1-b136-fae8c66f4f9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251089/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer-field/choices ["q-251089/field-1/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-251089/field-1/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251089" :question/id #uuid "c972b721-661a-53b1-be3e-5e738f66bd5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-251089" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/251ca3005dd302ec1e7ba0c7d7c497e28fd4c16cc0e431cc3691bdd4fe65446a.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{1}{5},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{1}{5}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5} & =\\frac{6x-1}{15x} \\\\ 15x & =5(6x-1) \\\\ 15x & =30x-5 \\\\ 15x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =15x=15(\\frac{1}{3})=5, \\\\ AC & =6x-1=6(\\frac{1}{3})-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251089/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251089"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251087/field-1/772faee3af740960f7d296ca245df4da797a9e413368076cbaa828915d92739d" :answer/id #uuid "86491e84-7a31-5e30-990e-33a0e59a7d7a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "128" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251087/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "130001a8-a8c5-56f9-81ea-43f1bd107e68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251087/field-1/772faee3af740960f7d296ca245df4da797a9e413368076cbaa828915d92739d" :answer-field/choices ["q-251087/field-1/772faee3af740960f7d296ca245df4da797a9e413368076cbaa828915d92739d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251087" :question/id #uuid "213eedb1-565d-5f76-b007-4e78dbc869a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-251087" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/05003be9090f98f39a65d9ec33e8568fa43ec5c427e34398e4932708f8a03ccc.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=4,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=4.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{11x-12}{x+4} \\\\ 4(x+4) & =11x-12 \\\\ 4x+16 & =11x-12 \\\\ 7x & =28 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =11x-12=11(4)-12=32, \\\\ AC & =x+4=4+4=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 32\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =128.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251087/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251087"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-28266"] :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=5.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{2x+4}{x-1} \\\\ 5(x-1) & =2x+4 \\\\ 5x-5 & =2x+4 \\\\ 3x & =9 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x+4=2(3)+4=10, \\\\ AC & =x-1=3-1=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-251086/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "1297785f-656c-5acc-9e1b-5dc1c3f4ba2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251086/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2b1d34d4-3efb-5490-a42e-fc7d33a1f42e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251086/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer-field/choices ["q-251086/field-1/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251086" :question/id #uuid "89d89b73-504a-5f33-91c3-a6a449c6798e" :question/math-academy-id "q-251086" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/51e60c645aa6be034a8ef23d16a9ca7a815ca15fe815d7c3b03a866e693f3e5b.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{3},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{3}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{10x-1}{8x+2} \\\\ 2(8x+2) & =3(10x-1) \\\\ 16x+4 & =30x-3 \\\\ 14x & =7 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =10x-1=10(\\frac{1}{2})-1=4, \\\\ AC & =8x+2=8(\\frac{1}{2})+2=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251086/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251086"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251121/field-1/e9bf0d8683d697a9168d9766312e0d9acef296c2f3ae0228f832eaed69a30a71" :answer/id #uuid "3a5fa6d7-3d77-55f1-aa75-b9f548fa982c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "225" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251121/field-1/e12f73422a456eca8c83cae70999c506825a539631c33c529fb793c051a91c96" :answer/id #uuid "0c086cd4-1d45-5818-901a-8e06b11d2b37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "450" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251121/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3e504436-4023-5f4b-99f4-15f12e0a9269" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251121/field-1/e9bf0d8683d697a9168d9766312e0d9acef296c2f3ae0228f832eaed69a30a71" :answer-field/choices ["q-251121/field-1/e9bf0d8683d697a9168d9766312e0d9acef296c2f3ae0228f832eaed69a30a71" "q-251121/field-1/e12f73422a456eca8c83cae70999c506825a539631c33c529fb793c051a91c96"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251121" :question/id #uuid "6e4f2531-54a0-5be4-a41b-03ab9dce1975" :question/math-academy-id "q-251121" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/214774fb428c62ad5131760c2a073690bca63f6b8bb06131c4381fee943597c3.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =2,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =2,$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ adjacent to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{BC}{15} \\\\ BC & =2\\cdot 15 \\\\ BC & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =225.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251121/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437a71fe-92e0-58e3-9f49-6560b2755776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251121"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124466/selection/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e" :answer/id #uuid "e3c3a4f1-4bd3-5fdb-9510-756ad4769b5d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "210" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124466/selection/1ad763bfa28dd8bf929699f6c31cff536336c19979c6baa533b7a886875a37b7" :answer/id #uuid "d7a25d3d-74ea-56ed-8931-14f46984d29a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "270" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124466/selection/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18" :answer/id #uuid "12e72070-ddac-5240-a4f3-e64f07645843" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "180" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124466/selection/557015e94af5fa4bd02ae0ff131d8572cb165f5648829317508c9b9e01215bfe" :answer/id #uuid "f0b35384-c99a-56ac-b1f5-ea1ceabfec87" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "240" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124466/selection/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c" :answer/id #uuid "01c1ef96-e707-5873-9dc2-04854dcb41ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "150" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124466/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0e9da70e-743e-522d-b545-2ea535a8382b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124466/selection/1ad763bfa28dd8bf929699f6c31cff536336c19979c6baa533b7a886875a37b7" :answer-field/choices ["q-124466/selection/407a8c9dd7706a5c0017938bdc16d552cb404ed5280e2197eaee2471cbb5128e" "q-124466/selection/1ad763bfa28dd8bf929699f6c31cff536336c19979c6baa533b7a886875a37b7" "q-124466/selection/23191a7abb2085fa58cfcf0bd067eedb8c4feb2e427bc3ee2024594244bb9b18" "q-124466/selection/557015e94af5fa4bd02ae0ff131d8572cb165f5648829317508c9b9e01215bfe" "q-124466/selection/42aff35720b567089407a2a0cf7c70ff6334c9493e4d877ecdcdfa86adae004c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124466" :question/id #uuid "ee965f67-bb44-5997-ae93-829735f50901" :question/math-academy-id "q-124466" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/4784e18b0e3631272efa1c002e686e9349ea04a900d8bc1e6b0416c09e994ccb.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{5}{3},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{5}{3},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AB}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3} & =\\frac{AC}{18} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\cdot 18 & =AC \\\\ AC & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =270.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124466/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437a71fe-92e0-58e3-9f49-6560b2755776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124466"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251130/field-1/97ed496329f58c9bb371237682450ecbf3f579a7995f64e3a2df22e7e40fdd2f" :answer/id #uuid "0c34f093-88d1-5c79-bea4-5cc38aeabc99" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251130/field-1/48a181b2b518efef2e708a1809dbe7a8771ecebba54d4cb9e50a234af2a10a62" :answer/id #uuid "cb248702-f541-551e-a9bf-d40ac94171d0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251130/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f41d44f4-bb54-5588-9a0b-9481c1ca932b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251130/field-1/97ed496329f58c9bb371237682450ecbf3f579a7995f64e3a2df22e7e40fdd2f" :answer-field/choices ["q-251130/field-1/97ed496329f58c9bb371237682450ecbf3f579a7995f64e3a2df22e7e40fdd2f" "q-251130/field-1/48a181b2b518efef2e708a1809dbe7a8771ecebba54d4cb9e50a234af2a10a62"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251130" :question/id #uuid "e75dd5d8-326f-57e3-93b1-3e0bc2ea6f68" :question/math-academy-id "q-251130" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/6b1c6c90b25fa7c4cd4cde42bdcd5e69a2ccef63f1945067a8f62dc7ee779f05.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7},$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ opposite to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the sine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{\\sqrt{13}}\\cdot 7 \\\\ AB & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}-(\\sqrt{13})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49-13} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-251130/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437a71fe-92e0-58e3-9f49-6560b2755776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251130"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251126/field-1/5048951f5787df5b4e66c729d300d473c2356e9097b4f01b088bd5252ede9c54" :answer/id #uuid "c98fc282-138a-506a-8540-d4695139aef2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251126/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "72938f94-b6fb-512e-adeb-21228d24c46d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251126/field-1/5048951f5787df5b4e66c729d300d473c2356e9097b4f01b088bd5252ede9c54" :answer-field/choices ["q-251126/field-1/5048951f5787df5b4e66c729d300d473c2356e9097b4f01b088bd5252ede9c54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251126" :question/id #uuid "3a1be4ef-1b5d-5162-b0ca-0628ac21678e" :question/math-academy-id "q-251126" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/ef2b0447e81370a50ea6d4115fc6f4687aff74fee17bc66f116b3c732667857e.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{7},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{7},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the cosine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} & =\\frac{4}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{4}{2}\\cdot 7 \\\\ AB & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{14}^{2}-{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{196-16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{180} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-251126/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437a71fe-92e0-58e3-9f49-6560b2755776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251126"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-28265"] :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2},$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ opposite to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the sine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{8}{AB} \\\\ AB & =8(2) \\\\ AB & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{16}^{2}-{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{256-64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{192} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot (8\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =32\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-76773/selection/010a31857cd90981948b13dae39c67c91e816b50728d36a2e9060ca306e6feab" :answer/id #uuid "748a0451-e2b6-5b99-8cdc-1231435460b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76773/selection/4bc417a7c6e4e85ed2389b791e422cb0d49f7bca20116d95266867feedd0bb73" :answer/id #uuid "4c8dc388-d96d-5441-8eac-e1515b0b6352" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76773/selection/5fb6be176de14df07c89e2bd4e2ececf4dc87d2f6d903730bb91fd1a73dfeb8a" :answer/id #uuid "bb6ee902-b8c8-53e4-a0de-fd12179780f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76773/selection/127f06aafda48787b3a8c9b5e8b9215260a70c483da41a5be92a3de54e74a3f4" :answer/id #uuid "0b01be37-6df9-5d3c-a931-4ca7bde9f76b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76773/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce" :answer/id #uuid "d23f457d-d71d-5f2b-b70e-3e38bab85939" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76773/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "38b0548b-65ba-5330-a819-cab72a3ac58a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76773/selection/127f06aafda48787b3a8c9b5e8b9215260a70c483da41a5be92a3de54e74a3f4" :answer-field/choices ["q-76773/selection/010a31857cd90981948b13dae39c67c91e816b50728d36a2e9060ca306e6feab" "q-76773/selection/4bc417a7c6e4e85ed2389b791e422cb0d49f7bca20116d95266867feedd0bb73" "q-76773/selection/5fb6be176de14df07c89e2bd4e2ececf4dc87d2f6d903730bb91fd1a73dfeb8a" "q-76773/selection/127f06aafda48787b3a8c9b5e8b9215260a70c483da41a5be92a3de54e74a3f4" "q-76773/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76773" :question/id #uuid "da752c15-1fa7-5b59-b50f-3601de203814" :question/math-academy-id "q-76773" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/ca9c6640b6cb239ae19b195731d8f605adae8826f66e10b075f7b0ad4a60690f.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+4} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+4} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(x+4) & =3\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\,x+4\\sqrt{3} & =3\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ -2\\sqrt{3}\\,x & =-4\\sqrt{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x=\\sqrt{3}(2)=2\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =x+4=2+4=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-76773/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76773"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76775/selection/9b223a0ab365daa4b5a2181b47705c4fbc769ef9e67ad9150396a67e2722390d" :answer/id #uuid "66da1f44-731a-5a09-a260-c29255faf8a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76775/selection/010a31857cd90981948b13dae39c67c91e816b50728d36a2e9060ca306e6feab" :answer/id #uuid "af187634-a302-5b48-8602-42eb66afceb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76775/selection/127f06aafda48787b3a8c9b5e8b9215260a70c483da41a5be92a3de54e74a3f4" :answer/id #uuid "01800aae-2f4b-5c50-8f93-57a557e1c1bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76775/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" :answer/id #uuid "657098f6-f4ad-5f2d-8a27-b485160682f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76775/selection/5fb6be176de14df07c89e2bd4e2ececf4dc87d2f6d903730bb91fd1a73dfeb8a" :answer/id #uuid "7bbc8320-f6d7-51f4-b226-cebb5d54794f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76775/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "19e5c726-5f44-5c16-93a4-0a873dc2a2c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76775/selection/5fb6be176de14df07c89e2bd4e2ececf4dc87d2f6d903730bb91fd1a73dfeb8a" :answer-field/choices ["q-76775/selection/9b223a0ab365daa4b5a2181b47705c4fbc769ef9e67ad9150396a67e2722390d" "q-76775/selection/010a31857cd90981948b13dae39c67c91e816b50728d36a2e9060ca306e6feab" "q-76775/selection/127f06aafda48787b3a8c9b5e8b9215260a70c483da41a5be92a3de54e74a3f4" "q-76775/selection/05402db46107d70ece210f0bd5e24b332ae4f43bd474d592035c3e3c92625629" "q-76775/selection/5fb6be176de14df07c89e2bd4e2ececf4dc87d2f6d903730bb91fd1a73dfeb8a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76775" :question/id #uuid "1386b559-f9dd-57ac-becb-7fb77e0e7576" :question/math-academy-id "q-76775" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/ab0e485908d86147b50e80f4d45c7e9966ab3453eb3ea01f6050bf1f7d88e2c8.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={60}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({60}^{∘}) & =\\frac{x+2}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{x+2}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3}\\,x) & =x+2 \\\\ 3x & =x+2 \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =x+2=1+2=3, \\\\ AB & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x=\\sqrt{3}(1)=\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-76775/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76775"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124475/selection/f169f92c1946b4a86dcd40a5cae1a30ea50a84a49ecc59038782fea0bf2058cc" :answer/id #uuid "8cf19cab-2d36-541e-b1e1-86d4871acc5e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124475/selection/127f06aafda48787b3a8c9b5e8b9215260a70c483da41a5be92a3de54e74a3f4" :answer/id #uuid "73fcb0dc-f733-515b-9bdd-bd69d99c2aff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124475/selection/d79808b1304c1856f3712e6e226ade34c7caf51f0407b91d3e2447e1f8a47743" :answer/id #uuid "72905faa-6ec6-5e72-aad8-deab943eb39b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124475/selection/010a31857cd90981948b13dae39c67c91e816b50728d36a2e9060ca306e6feab" :answer/id #uuid "703fe4a2-8381-563d-a086-8d740b5e8f9a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124475/selection/9b223a0ab365daa4b5a2181b47705c4fbc769ef9e67ad9150396a67e2722390d" :answer/id #uuid "1a730108-7698-514a-a07e-3658f58d2c20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124475/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c495a22-3a33-5b67-929e-2652b984c5bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124475/selection/9b223a0ab365daa4b5a2181b47705c4fbc769ef9e67ad9150396a67e2722390d" :answer-field/choices ["q-124475/selection/f169f92c1946b4a86dcd40a5cae1a30ea50a84a49ecc59038782fea0bf2058cc" "q-124475/selection/127f06aafda48787b3a8c9b5e8b9215260a70c483da41a5be92a3de54e74a3f4" "q-124475/selection/d79808b1304c1856f3712e6e226ade34c7caf51f0407b91d3e2447e1f8a47743" "q-124475/selection/010a31857cd90981948b13dae39c67c91e816b50728d36a2e9060ca306e6feab" "q-124475/selection/9b223a0ab365daa4b5a2181b47705c4fbc769ef9e67ad9150396a67e2722390d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124475" :question/id #uuid "963a40ef-ec42-5f96-ad58-c048d492c81f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124475" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/0ad5279a7ec9ac20a2c4e1449f93ae67854caf021aba8435165b80069f23afbd.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠B={60}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{AC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({60}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(x+2) & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\,x+2\\sqrt{3} & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x=2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2=4\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =x+2=2+2=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124475/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124475"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124471/selection/a92f495824787b0222a4590835652b83da05503f4172d766c87fc2a652f504ee" :answer/id #uuid "2a66f2ae-5e03-57b7-a978-dbdc33db814e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124471/selection/45f9c68d67f50b9d07653a9516f81d087414425a489a338a6744afb5b50241f3" :answer/id #uuid "fddca52e-d8ec-5acd-9f04-b74ff4127577" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124471/selection/7a9a0f552e5a9574e7415d028d83e4d2bc916f91557b773e49fe3910b966db7d" :answer/id #uuid "27248f76-3fcd-503e-8827-718b9ab3bd92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124471/selection/de1223d061b66c4875ebf8f846a1ca9d0b0e2e624356e6b1551c99ea0754f9a0" :answer/id #uuid "bfc3f6a0-4ad8-531b-a05a-d49e1e9d895e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15.6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124471/selection/b6d69a26b32de1fd096ce9b72c8761a665e81586bc6ad231c3f73e852707a0b9" :answer/id #uuid "969e0922-6fdc-522d-8dcd-0e7cbf944a51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124471/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bfeb9d4-a048-5bc6-a337-af552ccd8e41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124471/selection/45f9c68d67f50b9d07653a9516f81d087414425a489a338a6744afb5b50241f3" :answer-field/choices ["q-124471/selection/a92f495824787b0222a4590835652b83da05503f4172d766c87fc2a652f504ee" "q-124471/selection/45f9c68d67f50b9d07653a9516f81d087414425a489a338a6744afb5b50241f3" "q-124471/selection/7a9a0f552e5a9574e7415d028d83e4d2bc916f91557b773e49fe3910b966db7d" "q-124471/selection/de1223d061b66c4875ebf8f846a1ca9d0b0e2e624356e6b1551c99ea0754f9a0" "q-124471/selection/b6d69a26b32de1fd096ce9b72c8761a665e81586bc6ad231c3f73e852707a0b9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124471" :question/id #uuid "3fa83370-246b-52a5-bb67-0622bfb629ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-124471" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/f0d4e8ddf3a1b6cacab75f3207575695de5790f8223e30bc948e93daf37c939f.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, find the area of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{x-1}{x+2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})(x+2) & =x-1 \\\\ x\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =x-1 \\\\ x\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})-x & =-1-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})-1) & =-1-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ x(1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})) & =1+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})}{1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})} \\\\ x & =5.098\\,0…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =x-1=5.098\\,0-1=4.098\\,0…, \\\\ AB & =x+2=5.098\\,0+2=7.098\\,0….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(4.098\\,0…)(7.098\\,0…) \\\\  & =14.543\\,8… \\\\  & ≈14.5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124471/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124471"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124470/selection/4af97e5f5f97abbeb3c20369be44fa122e8adfaf9ef7b9583254ecdc87e84867" :answer/id #uuid "63eedc9b-db3e-581b-9940-2913e71e796e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "20\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124470/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" :answer/id #uuid "3e01d1a2-1c50-52e1-a59b-0070bde853a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124470/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" :answer/id #uuid "c3b6bea3-e9d9-50e5-a9b6-27e8f753a19f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "40" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124470/selection/f514d4c4087cf1f686a0e021f6ca20f520141ffab5968deed7a1d0b50b76b49d" :answer/id #uuid "dc38716b-0b31-5603-a6cc-89db61be99fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124470/selection/4bc417a7c6e4e85ed2389b791e422cb0d49f7bca20116d95266867feedd0bb73" :answer/id #uuid "7cf34dda-628b-57bd-b350-78befeae4976" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "24\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124470/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0745145-08f0-5e22-ba56-c5b6e3447a31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124470/selection/4bc417a7c6e4e85ed2389b791e422cb0d49f7bca20116d95266867feedd0bb73" :answer-field/choices ["q-124470/selection/4af97e5f5f97abbeb3c20369be44fa122e8adfaf9ef7b9583254ecdc87e84867" "q-124470/selection/713bb3b087b31554fba8b48520fba2f9d4d353e9b2d87f3d41c293daf48e1776" "q-124470/selection/695792c47319cb1ed098a6d83038b7ad6d032838f9103d693bf346f1dc234ff8" "q-124470/selection/f514d4c4087cf1f686a0e021f6ca20f520141ffab5968deed7a1d0b50b76b49d" "q-124470/selection/4bc417a7c6e4e85ed2389b791e422cb0d49f7bca20116d95266867feedd0bb73"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124470" :question/id #uuid "c661f073-d3a4-584b-af91-436e2a5fe0cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-124470" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/5c7116b4ee933aacb284e0d9b16576b910166bf1e01f58a46931fc0636a933c5.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{5x+2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{5x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(5x+2) & =3\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3}\\,x+2\\sqrt{3} & =6\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x=2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2=4\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =5x+2=5(2)+2=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot BC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =24\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-124470/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124470"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
